a2dp-ldac: build with the openvela LDAC library

The LDAC library published by openvela, the one with a decoder, declares
ldac_ABR_get_handle(const char *libpath). The older library in Android, which
bluez-alsa was written against, takes no argument. NULL keeps the old behaviour:
the adaptive bit rate module uses the LDAC functions it is linked with.

Only the sending side uses this call. Streamer only receives.

Upstream: not submitted; depends on which LDAC library is installed.

--- a/src/a2dp-ldac.c
+++ b/src/a2dp-ldac.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
 	pthread_cleanup_push(PTHREAD_CLEANUP(ldacBT_free_handle), handle);
 
 	HANDLE_LDAC_ABR handle_abr;
-	if ((handle_abr = ldac_ABR_get_handle()) == NULL) {
+	if ((handle_abr = ldac_ABR_get_handle(NULL)) == NULL) {
 		error("Couldn't get LDAC ABR handle: %s", strerror(errno));
 		goto fail_open_ldac_abr;
 	}
